    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1orc_1_1_lazy_object_linking_layer" kindref="compound">LazyObjectLinkingLayer</ref> is an adapter for <ref refid="classllvm_1_1orc_1_1_object_linking_layer" kindref="compound">ObjectLinkingLayer</ref> that builds lazy reexports for all function symbols in objects that are/ added to defer linking until the first call to a function defined in the object. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Linking is performed by emitting the object file via the base <ref refid="classllvm_1_1orc_1_1_object_linking_layer" kindref="compound">ObjectLinkingLayer</ref>.</para>
<para>No partitioning is performed: The first call to any function in the object will trigger linking of the whole object.</para>
<para>References to data symbols are not lazy and will trigger immediate linking (same os ObjectlinkingLayer). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
